      "JOYCE: A toothbrush! Do I recycle it? I don’t know. Twist-ties! Do I recycle them? I don’t know. A spent lightbulb. What in God’s name do I do with…\nJOYCE: Review your recycling guidelines, they’re not clear enough. There’s still a cell hole on Route 42 out past Sanger Landing. You can build a b…\nCOUNCILWOMAN WU: No it is not.\nSANDY: Good evening, council. The new cold storage facility near the highway is going to give our businesses a marvellous way to store their perish…",
      "SANDY: Joyce! How are you? Milt and I were just having a little dinner. Would you like to join?\nJOYCE: I seen the alien.",
      "SANDY: Well. Only when someone’s being dangerous toward us.\nJOYCE: Yeah. Only when someone’s being dangerous toward us.",
      "SANDY: Joyce?\nSANDY: Can I stay over your place? I’m scared to be alone, to be honest. And I’m not looking forward to going home to that mess.\nJOYCE: Of course.",
      "SANDY: It’s sort of a... rotting smell.\nJOYCE: I didn’t want to say anything. I thought it was maybe how your house usually smelled."
    ]
